  "type": "MCQ",
  "question": "Let $f(x)$ be a real-valued function satisfying $af(x)+bf(-x)=px^2+qx+r$, where $a$ and $b$ are distinct real numbers and $p,q,r$ are non-zero real numbers. Then $f(x)=0$ will have real solution when",
  "options": {
    "A": "$\\left(\\frac{a+b}{a-b}\\right)^2\\le\\frac{q^2}{4pr}$",
    "B": "$\\left(\\frac{a+b}{a-b}\\right)^2\\le\\frac{4pr}{q^2}$",
    "C": "$\\left(\\frac{a+b}{a-b}\\right)^2\\ge\\frac{q^2}{4pr}$",
    "D": "$\\left(\\frac{a+b}{a-b}\\right)^2\\ge\\frac{4pr}{q^2}$"
  },
  "answer": "D",
